          "reason": "The spec says 'client transaction SHOULD set timer F' and for timer E reset uses 'MUST' only for unreliable transport; the retransmission/reset behavior is described without explicit MUST for the reset itself — however the text says 'the timer is reset' which is normatively implied as MUST for unreliable transports. Actually the text says 'MUST set timer E' initially and 'the timer is reset' without explicit modal. But retransmission trigger says 'If an unreliable transport is in use, the client transaction MUST set timer E'. The reset is described as implicit. Keeping must is reasonable; but the original source uses no explicit modal for the reset action. Correcting to 'should' to match the implicit/descriptive tone."
